    "text": "To find the average number of birds seen by Marcus, Humphrey, and Darrel, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Sum the total number of birds seen by all three individuals:**\n   - Marcus sees 7 birds.\n   - Humphrey sees 11 birds.\n   - Darrel sees 9 birds.\n   - Total number of birds = 7 + 11 + 9 = 27.\n\n2. **Determine the number of individuals:**\n   - There are 3 individuals (Marcus, Humphrey, and Darrel).\n\n3. **Calculate the average number of birds seen per individual:**\n   - Average = Total number of birds / Number of individuals\n   - Average = 27 / 3 = 9.\n\nTherefore, the average number of birds seen by each of them is \\(\\boxed{9}\\).",
